- React 19.2.8 + TypeScript 6.0.3 + Vite 8 + Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`).
- HeroUI v3 (`@heroui/react` 3.2.4, `@heroui/styles` 3.2.4) — compound-component API built on react-aria-components 1.21.0 and tailwind-variants.
- react-router-dom 7.18.3 with `HashRouter`, `useSearchParams`, `useParams`, `useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `Navigate`, `Link`.
- Vitest 4.1.11 + jsdom + @testing-library/react 16 + user-event 14.
- URL `?state=` query as the only mechanism for pinning screen states; route wrapper components pass a `key` so state changes remount the page.
- RAC `ariaHideOutside`: multiple simultaneously-open overlays mutually set `aria-hidden`, so testing-library queries need `hidden: true` in that situation.
- RAC `FieldError` renders only when the field validation context `isInvalid` is true AND children are provided → pairs with controlled `isInvalid` on `TextField`.
- HeroUI variant vocabularies: Button variant = primary|secondary|tertiary|outline|ghost|danger|danger-soft (sizes sm|md|lg, no `color` prop); Chip color = accent|danger|default|success|warning, variant = primary|secondary|soft|tertiary; Alert status = accent|danger|default|success|warning; Card variant = default|secondary|tertiary|transparent; Table variant = primary|secondary; Drawer placement = bottom|left|right|top.
- HeroUI `Heading` accepts `level` (1–6) only — it maps internally to `type: h{level}` and renders the matching HTML element; passing `type` is a TypeScript error.
- HeroUI theme tokens exposed as Tailwind colors: `background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `surface`, `border`, `link`, `accent`, `danger`, `success`, `warning`, plus CSS vars `--background`, `--foreground` etc.
- `useOverlayState({defaultOpen})` → `{ isOpen, setOpen, open, close, toggle }`; `Modal`/`Drawer` take `state=`, `AlertDialog` takes `isOpen`/`onOpenChange` on the root (it forwards to RAC `DialogTrigger`).

